{
  "_INSTRUCTIONS": [
    "============================================================",
    "  HOW TO GET YOUR REAL credentials.json FROM GOOGLE",
    "============================================================",
    "",
    "STEP 1 — Create a Google Cloud Project:",
    "  → Go to: https://console.cloud.google.com/",
    "  → Click 'Select a project' → 'New Project'",
    "  → Name it: MindfulSpace (or anything you like)",
    "  → Click 'Create'",
    "",
    "STEP 2 — Enable the Google Calendar API:",
    "  → In your project, go to: APIs & Services → Library",
    "  → Search for 'Google Calendar API'",
    "  → Click it → Click 'Enable'",
    "",
    "STEP 3 — Create OAuth2 Credentials:",
    "  → Go to: APIs & Services → Credentials",
    "  → Click '+ Create Credentials' → 'OAuth client ID'",
    "  → If prompted, configure the OAuth consent screen first:",
    "      • User type: Internal (for college use) or External",
    "      • App name: MindfulSpace",
    "      • Add your email as developer contact",
    "      • Scopes: add 'Google Calendar API' → .../auth/calendar",
    "  → Application type: Desktop app (easiest for local dev)",
    "     OR Web application if deploying to a server",
    "  → Name: MindfulSpace Calendar Client",
    "  → Click 'Create'",
    "",
    "STEP 4 — Download the JSON file:",
    "  → After creation, click the download icon (⬇) next to your credential",
    "  → A file named 'client_secret_XXXX.json' will download",
    "  → Rename it to exactly: credentials.json",
    "  → Place it in the ROOT of this project (same folder as main.py)",
    "",
    "STEP 5 — Run the app and authorise:",
    "  → Run: python main.py",
    "  → Visit: http://localhost:5000/gcal-auth",
    "  → A browser tab will open → log in with the Google account",
    "    that OWNS the therapist calendars you want to access",
    "  → Grant calendar access permissions",
    "  → token.json will be auto-created in the project root",
    "  → You only need to do this ONCE (token auto-refreshes)",
    "",
    "STEP 6 — Set therapist calendar IDs:",
    "  → Each therapist's Google Calendar ID is usually their Gmail address",
    "  → Or go to: calendar.google.com → Settings → [calendar name] → Calendar ID",
    "  → Set these environment variables:",
    "     export GOOGLE_CALENDAR_T1='dr.mitchell@college.edu'",
    "     export GOOGLE_CALENDAR_T2='dr.okafor@college.edu'",
    "     export GOOGLE_CALENDAR_T3='dr.sharma@college.edu'",
    "     export GOOGLE_CALENDAR_P1='leo.thompson@college.edu'",
    "     export GOOGLE_CALENDAR_P2='amara.diallo@college.edu'",
    "     export GOOGLE_CALENDAR_P3='kai.nakamura@college.edu'",
    "",
    "STEP 7 — Verify everything works:",
    "  → Visit: http://localhost:5000/test-calendar",
    "  → You should see: ✅ CONNECTED with all checks passing",
    "",
    "============================================================",
    "  IMPORTANT SECURITY NOTES",
    "============================================================",
    "  • NEVER commit credentials.json or token.json to Git",
    "  • Add both to your .gitignore file immediately:",
    "      credentials.json",
    "      token.json",
    "  • For production: use Google Cloud Secret Manager or",
    "    environment variables instead of files on disk",
    "============================================================",
    "",
    "DELETE THIS FILE (credentials.json.example) after reading.",
    "The REAL credentials.json must NOT contain these instructions.",
    "It should look exactly like the template below."
  ],

  "_REAL_FILE_TEMPLATE": {
    "installed": {
      "client_id": "YOUR_CLIENT_ID.apps.googleusercontent.com",
      "project_id": "your-project-name",
      "auth_uri": "https://accounts.google.com/o/oauth2/auth",
      "token_uri": "https://oauth2.googleapis.com/token",
      "auth_provider_x509_cert_url": "https://www.googleapis.com/oauth2/v1/certs",
      "client_secret": "YOUR_CLIENT_SECRET",
      "redirect_uris": ["http://localhost"]
    }
  }
}
